 "confidence": 0.85,
 "evidence": "0x04 reads the same as 0x00 and 0x07 the same as 0x03 (only low 2 bits of register number used); register 2=0x00, register 3=0xF0; writing 0x0A to register 1 made register 0 read 0xFA; writing 0xFF to register 2 made it read 0x05; setting register 3=0x00 and register 1=0x00 with inversion on read 0xFF; not a PCF8574 (writing 0x00 did not change the pins)",
 "registers": "0 input (read-only), 1 output, 2 invert (1 = inverted), 3 direction (1 = input); only the low 2 bits of the register number count, so it repeats every 4 registers; reading many bytes repeats the same register",
